00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
Speaker 1: We're continuing our discussion around&nbsp;
gun violence that's been reignited due to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.640
recent mass shootings in Buffalo and Uvalde&nbsp;
and then a bunch of other mass shootings just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.600
since those, too. But one of the talking points&nbsp;
you'll hear the most, I think you've all probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.680
heard this. Whenever a tragedy, a tragedy like&nbsp;
this happens is it's not guns that kill people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.800
It's people that kills people. And at a really&nbsp;
fundamental level. Okay, that's true. Right?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.720
Guns don't fly around and shoot people. A person&nbsp;
has to pull the trigger. And oftentimes in every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.160
mass shooting, it is someone who is deranged and&nbsp;
has horrible motivations. All of that I agree to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:44.800
But what you and I understand and why we see that&nbsp;
slogan or that talking point to be so harmful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.920
is. The person who's already deranged has those&nbsp;
bad motivations, their ability to kill people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:59.840
And to kill a higher number of people comes&nbsp;
down to how effective of a killing tool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:05.600
a weapon they have to do that. And so at a&nbsp;
basic level, I think everyone understands this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.600
right? If I say you absolutely have to be&nbsp;
attacked, you have no choice. Someone's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.840
to attack you at your home. But you can decide&nbsp;
if it's going to be someone with just their bare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.240
